You can try the following, which looks like it will do what you want and 
time it in the process.  It rearranges the order of the subscripts. 
There is a way to get around that, but I don't remember it off the top 
of my head.  I'm pretty sure it's mentioned in Venables and Ripley, MASS.

tst<-array(rnorm(24), dim=c(2,3,4))
start.time <- proc.time()
tst.ranks <- apply(tst, 1:2, rank)
elapsed.time <- proc.time()-start.time
elapsed.time
dim(tst.ranks)
tst[1,1,]
tst.ranks[,1,1]

If you do the time comparison, I'd be interested in hearing the result.
Best Wishes,
Spencer Graves

