Subject: Re: Solution to merge problem
Message-ID: <OF8FAC2C4D.208CDA5A-ON86256CE1.004AE145@cr.usgs.gov>

All,
  I found that S-PLUS 6.1 merges timeDate data by converting it to
character first, merging, and then converting back to timeDate.  In order
to get an exact match between the two timeDate columns, the format slots
must be identical.  That can be done on the command line:
data1$datecolumn@format <- data2$datecolumn@format
  You must also be aware that the data are then sorted by the character
representation of the data, not the actual date.  The merged may need to be
by the timeDate column, either in the GUI or by the command line.
Dave

                                                                                
                                              
