Thanks to all who replied (responses shown below).  Once again, the
group provided timely and accurate assistance.  The combination of
the solutions provided by James Holtman and Bert Gunter resulted in a
reduction of the execution time to under 1.5 minutes.  I assumed the
upper.tri() function was a custom function or for illustrative purposes.
In addition to a bad cut and paste (noted by Patrick Burns) I had
violated a firm rule in S, namely let S do as much looping as
possible.  I had also worried, excessively it appears, about memory
"build-up" when looping over larger objects (the two 40x40
