Which version of S-PLUS are you using?

It does not happen in the current S-PLUS 6.1 (but your column names are 
not valid there)

It is the documented behaviour in S-PLUS <= 2000, and the documented
workaround is to use the I() operator.

Firing up Splus 3.4:

> ww1 <- matrix(T,6,2)
> dimnames(ww1) <- list(1:6, c("1M", "3M"))
> x <- data.frame(I(ww1))
> x
  I.ww1..1M I.ww1..3M 
1         T         T
2         T         T
3         T         T
4         T         T
5         T         T
6         T         T
> lapply(x, mode)
$I.ww1.:
[1] "logical"

or perhaps

x <- data.frame("1M"=I(ww1[,1]), "3M"=I(ww1[,2]), check.names=F)

