Gilliam, Reid wrote:
> Hi folks,
>
>
>
> I have a data frame in S-PLUS 6.1 from which I am trying to determine the
> row number with a particular value for a character column.
>
> Say my data frame named "SDF1" looks like this:
>
>
>
> Row   Value
> 1     "String1"
> 2     "String2"
> 3     "String3"
>
> where "Value" is the name of my character column.  What is the correct
> syntax to use to obtain "2" when I want to isolate the rows with the "Value"
> of "String2"?
>
> Right now, I'm using this:
>
>
>
> index.rowcol(SDF1,Value=="String2",which="rows")
>
>
>
> My output says: numeric(0)
>
>
>
> Why am I not getting 2 as my output?

Reid,
  Use matrix indexing:

SDF1[SDF1$Value=="String2", "Row"]

The first index isolates the row, the second index isolates the column. 
This assuming "Row" is actually a column in your data.frame and not the 
data.frame's `row.names' attribute. If the latter then use

row.names(SDF1)[SDF1$Value=="String2"]

Hope this helps.

Sundar

