P.J.Wells wrote:
> The following looks like it should be simple, but I can't see it -- would
> someone kick-start me?
>
> I have vectors sample.1, sample.2,...sample.N, where N is a random number,
> and length(sample.i) is also random.
>
> How do I turn these into one big vector?
Julian,
  There are several ways:

`for':
# assume each vector is named `sample.i'
# where `i' is 1:N
samp <- c()
for(i in 1:N)
  samp <- c(samp, get(paste("sample", i, sep = ".")))

`do.call':
# assume your N samples are in a list `samp.list'
# where length(samp.list) == N
samp <- do.call("c", samp.list)

HTH,
Sundar

