Subject: Hmisc and Design Libraries for S-Plus 6.x on Windows
Message-ID: <20030329080204.59271751.fharrell@virginia.edu>

Thanks to Chris Disdero, Lou Bajuk, and Michael O'Connell of Insightful 
Corportation, major updates to the Hmisc and Design libraries for Windows 
S-Plus 6.x are available at 
http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/s/Hmisc.html and
http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat/s/Design.html

To install these, delete [S-Plus Home]\library\Hmisc and [S-Plus 
Home]\library\Design and extract new .zip files into [S-Plus Home]\library as 
described in the installation instructions on the above web pages.  The web 
page containing the .zip files also contains change logs.

As this is the first time that .zip files updating Hmisc and Design for S-Plus 
6 on Windows have been made available, I would appreciate it if a few people 
installed the new versions soon and reported any problems to me.  Others may 
wish to wait several days before installing. 

The changes to the libraries consist of many bug fixes, some new functions 
(especially aregImpute for flexible multiple imputation), and many enhancements 
to old functions (especially for latex and summary.formula).  latex now should 
be compatible with MikTeX on Windows.  To use the new getHdata function for 
automatically accessing S-Plus datasets from our web site, you will need to 
install wget.exe as described in the documentation for getHdata.
-- 
Frank E Harrell Jr              Prof. of Biostatistics & Statistics
Div. of Biostatistics & Epidem. Dept. of Health Evaluation Sciences
U. Virginia School of Medicine  http://hesweb1.med.virginia.edu/biostat

